<title>ITALY: Italy has non-EU trade surplus in October.</title>
<headline>Italy has non-EU trade surplus in October.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy had a 5.919 trillion lire trade surplus with non-European Union countries in October, the national statistics office ISTAT said.</p>
<p>ITALY TRADE BALANCE (NON-EU) Oct 96    Sept 96	    Oct 95</p>
<p> Amount (lire)	     +5.919 trln   +1.501 trln   +3.087 trln</p>
<p> Imports		     11.358	  10.562 trln   11.698 trln</p>
<p> Exports		     17.277	  12.063 trln   14.785 trln</p>
<p> Cumulative yr to date +38.904 trln   +32.985 trln  +23.164 trln</p>
<p> Imports yr to date     104.697 trln   93.339 trln  109.618 trln</p>
<p> Exports yr to date     143.601 trln  126.324 trln  132.782 trln</p>
<p>Note: Sept 96 and Oct 95 figures were revised</p>
<p>Istat gave the following breakdown for the trade balance with European Union countries for September.</p>
<p>				  Sept 96     Aug 96	  Sept 95</p>
<p> Amount (lire)	    +1.349 trln   +1.062 trln   +2.056 trln</p>
<p> Imports		    16.677 trln   9.454 trln    17.775 trln</p>
<p> Exports		    18.026 trln   10.516 trln   19.811 trln</p>
<p>Note: August 96 and Sept 95 figures were revised</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
